<title>POLAND: Universal plans share buy-back, no payout.</title>
<headline>Universal plans share buy-back, no payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish trading company Universal SA plans to earmark a portion of its 1996 profits for share buy-back, the company said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Universal, which showed a net profit of 23 million zlotys last year, plans no dividend payout and said it would set split its earnings between reserve capital, the buy-back scheme, bonuses for supervisory board members and a fund for employees.</p>
<p>It said the management's proposal has yet to be approved by its general shareholders meeting and the management would later announce the detailed breakdown of the funds' allocation. @</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment. Universal did not pay a 1995 dividend.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
